I got the following additional comments from a member of the HP Tru64 =
Unix SSH team that I thought might be useful to the group.

In summary, the SSH v3.2.0 installed with Tru64 5.1b-3 is actually a =
later build than the SSH v3.2.3 on the HP website, and even though the =
website download is marked as being for "Tru64 5.1a or later" it is =
actually intended for "Tru64 5.1a ONLY".


"
Please be aware that the SSH kit available via the HP website is for use =
on a V5.1A systems ONLY.

The SSH that is available with the Tru64 5.1B-3 (pk5) contains all of =
the latest fixes available for our SSH.  The SSH that ships as part of =
HP Tru64 Unix V5.1B is based on the SSH toolkit version 3.2.0 from =
SafeNET (was SSH communications, see www.ssh.com).

Due to legal reasons, the version number you see when you do "ssh -V" is =
the SSH toolkit version number 3.2.0, but our SSH has some additional =
functionality and fixes.  We continue to release patches to the SSH bits =
as part of the aggregate patch kits.=20
"



