Yet another file which you're not supposed to touch,
or you'll disrupt future patch kit installation -
Tru64 patch management never stops surprising me...

The file /etc/pmgrd_iorate.config should be a soft link to
../cluster/members/{memb}/etc/pmgrd_iorate.config
which I had somehow overwritten.  Recreating the soft
link by
   cd /etc; ln -s '../cluster/members/{memb}/etc/pmgrd_iorate.config'
(notice the quotes to escape {memb}) fixes the problem.
Now I could let dupatch do a baseline check without error.

Thanks to these people for the correct answer:
    "Dr Thomas.Blinn@HP.com" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>
    "Jenny Butler" <jbutler@utmem.edu>
    "A. Mahendra Rajah" <Mahendra.Rajah@URegina.CA>
    "Brusche, Johan" <johan.brusche@hp.com>

> I'm trying to upgrade Tru64 5.1B from patch kit 4 to patch kit 5.
> There's an error which I haven't been able to solve (see below).
> The file /etc/pmgrd_iorate.config was modified by me for disk
> monitoring, so I've renamed this file prior to installing the patch kit.
> I've also done a dupatch baseline operation, but this didn't
> solve the problem with /etc/pmgrd_iorate.config.
> 
> Any suggestions for a resolution ?  At the moment that patch
